  "tags": ["event-driven", "architecture", "fundamentals"],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "Event-driven architecture (EDA) uses events to communicate between services. Instead of direct requests, services publish events and other services react to them."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Key Concepts"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "key-terms",
      "data": {
        "terms": [
          {
            "term": "Event",
            "definition": "A fact that something happened in the system."
          },
          {
            "term": "Event Producer",
            "definition": "A service that publishes events."
          },
          {
            "term": "Event Consumer",
            "definition": "A service that subscribes to and reacts to events."
          },
          {
            "term": "Event Broker",
            "definition": "Middleware that routes events between producers and consumers."
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Event-Driven vs Request-Driven"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "data": {
        "headers": ["Aspect", "Request-Driven", "Event-Driven"],
        "rows": [
          ["Communication", "Direct request/response", "Publish/subscribe"],
          ["Coupling", "Tight (caller knows callee)", "Loose (producer does not know consumers)"],
          ["Timing", "Synchronous", "Asynchronous"],
          ["Scalability", "Limited", "High"]
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Event Types"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "bullet-list",
      "data": {
        "items": [
          "Domain events: business events (OrderPlaced)",
          "Integration events: cross-service events",
          "System events: infrastructure events (deployment)"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Benefits"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "bullet-list",
      "data": {
        "items": [
          "Loose coupling between services",
          "Better scalability",
          "Services can react independently",
          "Easier to add new consumers"
        ]
      }
    },
